The meshes under models/myagv_mecharm/meshes/ come from Elephant Robotics,
see LICENSE in this directory for both licenses.

myagv_body, myagv_top and myagv_wheel_* were generated from myagv_base.dae
and myagv_up.dae in https://github.com/elephantrobotics/myagv_ros2
(myagv_description), Copyright (c) 2024 Elephant Robotics, BSD-3-Clause.
The four mecanum wheels were split out of the base mesh so they can turn,
and everything was converted from inches to meters.

mecharm_* and gripper_* were converted to STL in meters from the mechArm 270 Pi
and adaptive gripper meshes in https://github.com/elephantrobotics/mycobot_ros2
(mycobot_description), Copyright (c) 2020 Elephant Robotics, BSD-2-Clause.

The arm and gripper joint origins, axes and limits in
myagv_mecharm_common.urdf.xacro follow mecharm_270_pi_adaptive_gripper.urdf
from the same source. The driving gripper joint is renamed from
gripper_controller to gripper_base_to_gripper_left3 because ros2_control
cannot activate a controller named like one of its joints. The laser and
camera frames follow the myAGV bringup in
https://github.com/elephantrobotics/myagv_ros (myagv_odometry).

The myagv_mycobot robot in this repository reuses the myAGV and gripper
meshes from this directory.

Everything else in this directory is original work for RoboticsAcademy.
